<header><p class="enc-kicker"><a href="/encyclopedia/conflicts/20th-century">Conflicts &amp; Resolutions</a> · Revolution</p><h1 class="enc-title">Carnation Revolution</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">1974</span> · <a href="/centuries/20th-century">20th century</a></p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Carnation Revolution was a largely bloodless military coup in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/lisbon">Lisbon</a> on 25 April 1974 that overthrew the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/estado-novo-portugal">Estado Novo</a> dictatorship in Portugal. Its leaders were partly motivated by the costly colonial wars in <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. The new democratic government rapidly decolonised Portugal's African territories, bringing the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/portuguese-empire">Portuguese Empire</a> to an end.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/carnation-revolution.jpg" alt="Carnation Revolution" width="314" height="420" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Unknown authorUnknown author · CC BY 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Revolu%C3%A7%C3%A3o_dos_Cravos.jpg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
